REQUIRED ATTRIBUTION  (how the BY term is satisfied for THIS work)
----------------------------------------------------------------

Any copy, redistribution, or extension of this work MUST:

  1. Credit "Serendip Commons Society" as steward and publisher of the work.

  2. Retain and carry forward the file CONTRIBUTORS.md, reproducing the
     contributor list exactly as it stood in the version you copied or
     extended — i.e. "the contributor list at the time of extension."
     You MAY append new contributors; you may NOT remove or alter existing
     entries.

  3. Retain this copyright notice and the license notice, and provide a link
     back to the source repository (or its DOI).

  4. State that changes were made, if you modified the work, and keep your
     derivative under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.

Suggested attribution line:

    Based on "Philosophy of Intimacy and the Theory of Justice" by
    Serendip Commons Society and its contributors (see CONTRIBUTORS.md),
    licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. Changes, if any, are indicated.

----------------------------------------------------------------
COMMERCIAL USE  (forbidden by default; permitted only by separate license)
----------------------------------------------------------------

The NonCommercial term means commercial use is forbidden IN PRINCIPLE under the
free public grant. It is permitted only as an EXCEPTION, by separate license
from Serendip Commons Society obtained BEFORE the use.

  - Whether to grant a commercial license, and on what terms (scope, fees,
    attribution, revenue sharing, etc.), is decided by Serendip Commons Society
    according to its own bylaws and commercial-licensing policy, as amended
    from time to time. Those rules — not this file — govern the procedure.

  - The Society can license the work as a whole, including third-party
    contributions, because every contributor grants it that right via the
    inbound contributor grant in CONTRIBUTORS.md.

  Commercial-licensing enquiries: Serendip Commons Society
  (huangwanhong.g.official@gmail.com; see huang-wanhong.com).

Net effect: the public always keeps the free, non-commercial CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
freedoms, while every commercial use flows through a single authority — the
Society — under rules the Society sets.

