RESERVATION OF RIGHTS  (the copyright holders are NOT bound by NC / SA)
----------------------------------------------------------------

The CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 grant above runs to the PUBLIC and is NON-EXCLUSIVE. It
restricts licensees; it does not restrict the copyright holders. Serendip
Commons Society and the authors retain full copyright in their own material
and all rights not expressly granted to the public.

In particular, the copyright holders MAY, without limitation:
  - publish, print, sell, or otherwise commercially exploit the work,
    including the founder's own original edition(s) of this book;
  - grant separate commercial or other licenses to third parties (for example,
    a publisher) on negotiated terms; and
  - release further versions under different terms.

Publishing a commercial edition of the original work AND also releasing the
work to the public under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 — whether at the same time or one
after the other (e.g. commercial first, open afterward) — is expressly
permitted and is the intended model here. The public CC grant neither waives
nor diminishes these reserved rights.

These reserved rights cover each holder's OWN material. A commercial edition
that also incorporates third-party contributions made to the open version
relies, in addition, on the inbound contributor grant described in
CONTRIBUTORS.md.

